        itemId = 46817,
        name = "Silver Covenant Tabard",
        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Unlock the appropriate tournament championship, earn Exalted reputation and buy the tabard with seals.\n\n1. On an eligible Alliance character, check The Silver Covenant reputation and whether Hiren Loresong will sell to you. If already unlocked and Exalted, skip the training and reputation stages, then collect the 50 purchase seals.\n\n2. If new to the tournament, speak to Justicar Mariel Trueheart in Icecrown (69.6, 22.8), then Arcanist Taelis in your faction pavilion (76.2, 19.4). Complete the lance and mounted-combat lessons. For jousts, equip the lance, use a tournament mount, refresh Defend, strip enemy shields with Shield-Breaker and Charge when there is room.\n\n3. Finish Up to the Challenge: collect 15 Aspirant's Seals from the pavilion's training dailies, normally five per day, then complete The Aspirant's Challenge. Advance a city's A Valiant's Charge with 25 Valiant's Seals, complete The Valiant's Challenge and A Champion Rises. These training seals unlock progression; keep them separate from Champion's Seals.\n\n4. Raise The Silver Covenant to Exalted through the pavilion's available Valiant and Champion quests. Combine the rotating weapon errand with field training, The Grand Melee/Among the Champions and At the Enemy's Gates/Battle Before the Citadel when offered. Completing further city championships advances this reputation while working toward Crusader. Check this exact faction's bar, not the city or Argent Crusade bar.\n\n5. Optional dungeon reputation: remove ALL reputation-championing tabards and clear original Wrath heroics, such as Halls of Lightning in the Storm Peaks (45.4, 21.4). Check The Silver Covenant directly before and after: chat can emphasize Alliance Vanguard/Horde Expedition or another subfaction while this reputation also rises. Wearing an unrelated reputation tabard diverts those gains.\n\n6. Save 50 Champion's Seals from unlocked Champion dailies and their purses. The Black Knight investigation through The Black Knight's Fall unlocks Threat From Above. For additional seals, do the daily Heroic Trial of the Champion clear at the five-player Coliseum entrance (75.1, 21.8 in Icecrown). This is not the Trial of the Crusader raid entrance.\n\n7. At Exalted, visit Hiren Loresong inside the Alliance pavilion (76.2, 19.6 in Icecrown). Buy Silver Covenant Tabard for 50 Champion's Seals. Check that you do not already own it: buying another copy is possible and wastes seals.\n\n8. Equip the tabard and confirm the Wardrobe appearance. Keep the purchase; the item cannot be returned for a seal refund and ordinary tabard designers do not provide a free replacement for a discarded tournament purchase.",
