        },
        itemId = 49052,
        name = "Tabard of Conquest",
        stepCount = 13,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Finish the Isle of Conquest meta, including 100 wins and coordinated bomb, vehicle and objective criteria.\n\n1. Track Master of Isle of Conquest (3857) on an eligible Alliance character. Expand its missing subachievements. Queue for Isle of Conquest through PvP, or use Random Epic Battlegrounds. Work on the objectives below during matches while building the win total.\n\n2. Isle of Conquest Veteran: win 100 games. Keep this counter running while doing the specialized criteria. Losses can advance many other objectives, but they do not add victories.\n\n3. Four Car Garage: personally control a Glaive Thrower and Catapult from the Docks, plus a Demolisher and Siege Engine from the Workshop. Enter the appropriate controlling seat and verify each criterion; sitting only in a passenger or gunner seat may not give the required control credit.\n\n4. Back Door Job: enter the ENEMY courtyard while its gates are still intact. Use a Docks catapult to launch over the wall, or the Hangar's gunship to parachute in. Do this before your team breaks a gate; walking through an already destroyed gate does not meet the condition.\n\n5. A-bomb-inable and A-bomb-ination: in one battle, use 5 ordinary Seaforium Bombs on enemy gates; separately, in one battle, use 5 HUGE Seaforium Bombs. Ordinary bombs come from the Workshop; huge bombs are inside the enemy courtyard. Pick up the correct type, carry it to an intact enemy gate, plant it and let it detonate. Refill and repeat, watching each separate counter. A disarmed bomb may not give the required damage credit.\n\n6. Cut the Blue Wire... No the Red Wire!: disarm 25 enemy bombs, accumulated across games. Defend your own gates, watch for a planted explosive, then interact and finish the disarm before it explodes. Crowd-control attackers or ask teammates to cover you; damage or movement can interrupt the cast. Stay for defensive opportunities even in a losing game.\n\n7. Mowed Down: while using a keep turret, collect 100 player kills and destroy 10 vehicles. Player honorable-kill credit can count, but recent replies stress that vehicles require the turret's finishing damage. Watch the vehicle counter after each destruction instead of assuming a nearby teammate's kill counted.\n\n8. Demolition Derby: destroy an enemy Glaive Thrower, Catapult, Demolisher and Siege Engine. Hunt Docks and Workshop vehicles, participate directly in their destruction and verify all four checkmarks. These are destruction objectives, separate from controlling your own team's vehicles.\n\n9. Glaive Grave: use a Glaive Thrower to kill 10 players without dying. Keep the vehicle protected and aim at enemy players instead of only gates. Ask teammates for cover and repairs; a fast vehicle loss can ruin the attempt before the required streak.\n\n10. All Over the Isle: in a SINGLE battle, obtain player-kill credit at the Workshop, Docks, Hangar, Alliance Keep and Horde Keep. Check each location during the same match and travel to missing sites before it ends. Kills split across separate battles do not finish this criterion.\n\n11. Mine: win while your team simultaneously CONTROLS the Quarry, Refinery, Docks/Shipyard, Workshop and Hangar. An assaulted flag is not a fully controlled node. Coordinate the last captures and protect all five until the winning moment; merely capturing each once during the match is insufficient.\n\n12. When every required subachievement completes, collect the mailed Tabard of Conquest. If mail is delayed, or an alt needs its faction copy, speak to Elizabeth Ross in Northrend Dalaran (51.6, 55.4) and choose the lost-Tabard-of-Conquest dialogue. Later replies explicitly correct the old claim that it cannot be reclaimed.\n\n13. Equip the tabard and check the learned appearance. Its Alliance and Horde looks differ; a Conquest currency purchase or the ordinary Orgrimmar/Stormwind tabard is not this reward.",
        sourceType = "PvP",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=49052",
        difficultyReason = "Finish the Isle of Conquest meta, including 100 wins and coordinated bomb, vehicle and objective criteria.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
